WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.012
Every decision gets one owner.

2
00:00:02.012 --> 00:00:06.235
The executive sponsor and the CIO
own scope, funding and sequence,

3
00:00:06.235 --> 00:00:09.988
and they decide when Active
Directory components retire.

4
00:00:09.988 --> 00:00:12.550
The CISO sets the control requirements.

5
00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:17.037
The steward runs the program office
and owns the plan and the repository.

6
00:00:17.037 --> 00:00:22.353
Each gate is signed by whoever matches
what it ends: the steward clears most of

7
00:00:22.353 --> 00:00:27.501
them, and the sponsor and CIO sign the
last one, the one that says AD is retired.

8
00:00:27.501 --> 00:00:31.814
The book corrects the plans on three
decisions, and one matters most:

9
00:00:31.814 --> 00:00:35.512
residual risk belongs to the
authorizing official alone.

10
00:00:35.512 --> 00:00:39.146
Under the Risk Management Framework
no one else can accept it,

11
00:00:39.146 --> 00:00:42.851
and for federal agencies it's an
inherently governmental role.

12
00:00:42.851 --> 00:00:44.125
And plan for people.

13
00:00:44.125 --> 00:00:48.417
The core team is about five and a
half full-time staff, and the budget

14
00:00:48.417 --> 00:00:52.850
has to cover others too, like
application owners, the help desk and HR.
